facts:
  - "WhatsApp's limits are confusing because the app treats the same file three ways. Sent from the gallery or video button it allows up to 2GB but re-encodes it. Sent with the paperclip as a document it keeps the original quality, with a smaller cap. Older guides saying a flat 16MB are out of date."
  - "The size is rarely the real problem. The re-encoding is. WhatsApp squeezes video down to roughly 720p with settings tuned for slow connections, so a clip that looked sharp arrives soft. Compressing it yourself first means you pick the trade-off. At 16MB, a 16:9 video stays at 720p up to about 59 seconds, and at 480p up to about 2 minutes."
  - "On most phones, tap Share when it finishes to send the video straight to WhatsApp."
